playstyle{3 \\choose 3}.$" 13194139538225 17592186576411 true] [17592186171810 1074 "The binomial coefficient $\\displaystyle{n \\choose r}$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{n \\choose r} = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,  r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n = 5$ and $r = 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5}{4}) & =\\frac{5!}{(5-4)!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4!}{1!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538225 17592186576411 false] [17592186171810 1074 "The binomial coefficient $\\displaystyle{n \\choose r}$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{n \\choose r} = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,  r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n = 5$ and $r = 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right) & =\\frac{5!}{(5-4)!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4!}{1!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538225 17592186576411 true] [17592186171824 1074 "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^2 = 4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-10x-4y-7 & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-10x & =4y+7 \\\\ 5[{x}^{2}-2x] & =4y+7 \\\\ 5[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =4y+7 \\\\ 5(x-1)^{2}-5 & =4y+7 \\\\ 5(x-1)^{2} & =4y+7+5 \\\\ 5(x-1)^{2} & =4y+12 \\\\ 5(x-1)^{2} & =4(y+3) \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{4}{5}(y+3) \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{5})(y+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k) = (1,-3).$" 13194139538225 17592186576411 false] [17592186171824 1074 "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^2 = 4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-t