ht)+\\operatorname{sin}x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}x-\\operatorname{cos}x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538225 17592186576411 true] [17592186234047 1071 "Express $6\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})$ as a single trigonometric ratio." 13194139538225 17592186576411 false] [17592186234047 1071 "Express $6\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio." 13194139538225 17592186576411 true] [17592186234047 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{10})=\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})=3\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})=3\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{5}).\n$$" 13194139538225 17592186576411 false] [17592186234047 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{10})=\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{5}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}\\right)=3\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{10}\\right)=3\\operatorname{sin